      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-287600",
      ":question/problem": "A farmer is mixing two types of feed. One feed provides $\\frac{2}{3}$ pound of protein per unit and the other provides $\\frac{5}{6}$ pound of protein per unit. The equation $\\frac{2}{3}x + \\frac{5}{6}y = 7$ models the total pounds of protein provided by $x$ units of the first feed and $y$ units of the second feed. If $3$ units of the first feed were used, how many units of the second feed were used?"
